y_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19837, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01X4svzNKd6mKqMNhEsjdLz8", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19837, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_016zi4yC9WDsDMbedLGcfyQ6", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20137, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016zi4yC9WDsDMbedLGcfyQ6", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20137, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016zi4yC9WDsDMbedLGcfyQ6", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25401, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01P4BB5NAAqRsNybwPfZkGsz", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. The SRE agent rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollout. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error during rollback, and find out why v2.3.1 was promoted when its RC was unhealthy in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56001, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01P4BB5NAAqRsNybwPfZkGsz", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56001, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01P4BB5NAAqRsNybwPfZkGsz", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57844, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01EhX7K3agLSQK5CN8tEVJSc", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58144, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01EhX7K3agLSQK5CN8tEVJSc", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58144, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EhX7K3agLSQK5CN8tEVJSc", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63260, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as **INC-0001**.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was unhealthy, and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed in staging.\n  - The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1.\n  - I retried with the same target version, which was safe to repeat, and the rollout finished.\n- **Current state:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to open it timed out. Before trying again I checked the incident list and found it had already been created, so there's no duplicate and the on-call engineer was paged only once.\n  - It describes the failure, the rollback (including the orchestrator error) and three follow-ups: why v2.3.1 failed, what caused the orchestrator error, and why v2.3.1 shipped when its release candidate had failed in staging.\n\nNo approval was needed, since v2.3.0 had been healthy in production before.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018fV7UPdWYvdmRZdND9JGLG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LuE2K8ppViyXzHNjMHDpiV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01BMKVBLT7Mxxr3Nn6ugW6ci", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Gi8Cok8ZN9B1pvozHrb17F", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: only us-east is on v2.3.0. Running it again is safe because it targets the same version, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_011e6vFppjS8zVw87UE8vfKy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01X4svzNKd6mKqMNhEsjdLz8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016zi4yC9WDsDMbedLGcfyQ6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01P4BB5NAAqRsNybwPfZkGsz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. The SRE agent rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollout. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error during rollback, and find out why v2.3.1 was promoted when its RC was unhealthy in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01EhX7K3agLSQK5CN8tEVJSc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as **INC-0001**.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was unhealthy, and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed in staging.\n  - The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1.\n  - I retried with the same target version, which was safe to repeat, and the rollout finished.\n- **Current state:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to open it timed out. Before trying again I checked the incident list and found it had already been created, so there's no duplicate and the on-call engineer was paged only once.\n  - It describes the failure, the rollback (including the orchestrator error) and three follow-ups: why v2.3.1 failed, what caused the orchestrator error, and why v2.3.1 shipped when its release candidate had failed in staging.\n\nNo approval was needed, since v2.3.0 had been healthy in production before.", "type": "text"}]}]}